{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1157176-sons-of-borr","id":1157176,"title":"Sons of Borr","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-08T19:13:36-08:00","id":1157176,"title":"Sons of Borr","content":"So I'm curious about people's interpretations of Norse Myth, as it may play out at the Scion table. Do you see Odin as having two birth-brothers aside from Loki as an adopted brother, as would be implied by Loki's jabs about Ve and Vili marrying/bedding Frigg in the Lokasenna? If so, and the three sons of Borr slew Ymir and forged the world, do you prefer the Prose Eddas telling where they are also the three creators of mankind? The Poetic Eddas attribute that to Odin, Hoenir, and Lodurr? Or do you think Hoenir and Lodurr are the same figures as Vili and Ve (this matter is confused by a significant number of scholars arguing Lodurr is a name of Loki)?<br /> <br /> There are also scenes of Odin, Hoenir, and Loki as traveling companions - so if that's a significant triad perhaps Hoenir = Vili, while Loki = Lodurr = Ve? Loki himself has two named brothers in myth, Byleister and Helbindi. Helbindi is often read as a sobriquet of Odin, so if Byleister is Hoenir/Vili, that composits us down to only one relative mystery figure.<br /> <br /> Of course, all of this raises the question of what is meant by Loki being Odin's &quot;blood-brother&quot; as he has different listed parents. Loki could be a blood-oath sword adopted son of Borr I suppose.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T16:24:40-08:00","id":1157389,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the Hoenir = Vili and Lodurr = Ve as it solves the question of &quot;what happened to Odin's brothers&quot; and fleshes out Hoenir's character who has a lot of interesting stuff going on but is still pretty obscure. Lodurr = Loki I'm not totally sold on, because it conflicts with other sources. It does kind of explain why Loki's giant family never really shows up though, seeing as they would have died with the other giants in the blood-flood.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T09:27:06-08:00","id":1157770,"title":"","content":"The matter is further frustrated by the fact that the actual Norse for the trait that Hoenir or Vili (depending on the telling) gave Ask and Embla is &quot;Odr&quot; (no great English translation, can mean poetic inspiration, spiritual insight, battle frenzy, etc)...<br /> <br /> - Odin's name literally derives from Odr! So why isn't he granting it if Vili/Hoenir is a separate god?<br /> <br /> - Odr is also given as he name of Freyja's missing (presumably Vanir?) husband","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T10:48:22-08:00","id":1157782,"title":"","content":"My current idea is to just go ahead an say &quot;Snorri got it wrong, Odin gave Odr, Vili/Hoenir gave animating life, and Ve/Lodurr gave form&quot;.<br /> <br /> Then portray Vili/Hoenir is a god of physical life, a mighty warrior, and force of unstoppable will in the direction he's pointed in - though obviously not a decisive leader to know where to direct that will. While Ve/Lodurr was the artisan of the Aesir, who faded from relevance because of Loki introducing superior dwarven crafts (see the Mjolnir origin myth)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}